video: let a port offer the sizes it can show, not only the ten upstream named

SheepShaver's native video driver answers the Display Manager's
cscGetNextResolution from VModes, but it stops at APPLE_ID_MAX, which is
APPLE_CUSTOM: ten identifiers, all 4:3 or thereabouts, and a single free one.
A port on a 16:9 display therefore cannot list 1280x720, 1600x900, 1920x1080
or 2560x1440 beside each other, although nothing in the Mac's protocol limits
the identifiers to those ten. Basilisk II's driver answers the same call and
walks every identifier up to 0xff (BasiliskII/src/video.cpp:862).

Three changes, none of which alters what an existing port sees:

- APPLE_ID_MAX becomes 0xff. The walk still skips every identifier VModes
  does not hold, so a port that only uses the named ten lists exactly what it
  listed before.
- The size reported for an identifier with no named case comes from VModes,
  as APPLE_CUSTOM's already did. Named identifiers keep their written sizes
  and refresh rates. cscGetModeTiming already had a default, timingUnknown and
  valid, so the Monitors control panel shows the new sizes as it shows the
  custom one.
- VModes grows from 64 entries to VIDEO_MODES_MAX, 128, and says so in the
  header: fifteen sizes at six depths is 90 entries, and a port has to know
  the capacity to stay inside it.

Okapia offers both of its Macintosh the same list of sizes, and this is what
lets the PowerPC one carry it.

diff --git a/SheepShaver/src/include/video.h b/SheepShaver/src/include/video.h
index 678e5777..6ea6beba 100644
--- a/SheepShaver/src/include/video.h
+++ b/SheepShaver/src/include/video.h
@@ -35,6 +35,9 @@ struct VideoInfo {
 	uint32 viAppleID;		// Screen DisplayID
 };
 
+// Room for every size a port offers at every depth, and the end marker.
+enum { VIDEO_MODES_MAX = 128 };
+
 extern struct VideoInfo VModes[];	// List of available video modes
 
 enum {	// viAppleMode
@@ -92,7 +95,10 @@ enum {	// viAppleID
 	APPLE_1600x1200,
 	APPLE_CUSTOM,
 	APPLE_ID_MIN = APPLE_640x480,
-	APPLE_ID_MAX = APPLE_CUSTOM
+	// A port may number sizes of its own past APPLE_CUSTOM: the driver lists
+	// whatever VModes holds, up to the same 0xff that Basilisk II's driver
+	// walks to (BasiliskII/src/video.cpp:862).
+	APPLE_ID_MAX = 0xff
 };
 
 enum {	// Display type
diff --git a/SheepShaver/src/video.cpp b/SheepShaver/src/video.cpp
index c4da320a..8727ecf0 100644
--- a/SheepShaver/src/video.cpp
+++ b/SheepShaver/src/video.cpp
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@ bool keyfile_valid;		// Flag: Keyfile is valid, enable full-screen modes
  *  Video mode information (constructed by VideoInit())
  */
 
-struct VideoInfo VModes[64];
+struct VideoInfo VModes[VIDEO_MODES_MAX];
 
 
 /*
@@ -848,7 +848,7 @@ static int16 VideoStatus(uint32 pb, VidLocals *csSave)
 					WriteMacInt32(param + csVerticalLines, 1200);
 					WriteMacInt32(param + csRefreshRate, 75<<16);
 					break;
-				case APPLE_CUSTOM: {
+				default: {		// APPLE_CUSTOM, and any size a port numbered itself
 					uint32 x, y;
 					get_size_of_resolution(work_id, x, y);
 					WriteMacInt32(param + csHorizontalPixels, x);
